/ json (2026-11-01): json x parses JSON text (a char vector) into gk data and serializes
/ anything else as JSON text.  object -> dict (keys must be names), array -> list, an
/ all-numeric array -> typed vector of the widest member with null as its null,
/ string -> chars, number -> int if it fits i32, long if i64, else float (a fraction or
/ exponent is always a float), true/false -> 1/0, null -> nul.  Writing: numbers as 5:
/ prints them at \p (a float always carries a point or exponent; nulls and infinities ->
/ null), symbols and char atoms -> strings, functions -> type error.
